                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Lots of wasted potential. As other reviewers have already pointed out, this game offers mostly stealth missions and control of small groups of soldiers. The stealth missions and mechanics are not well designed and that takes away from the experience. I really enjoyed the previous entries int he Men of War series. Vietnam was a great setting to take the game into but the execution feels lazy, there are no pitched battles, vehicle combat is worse than before and the game is over before it started (the only thing dragging it out is the grinding nature of some of these missions. The way the game is designed feels like save scumming is encouraged.)",
